# Build context exclusions. NOTE: this file can cancel a COPY in the Dockerfile
# -- exclude `frontend/` here and the /ui mount serves 404s from an image that
# looks correctly built. tests/test_image_contents.py reads BOTH lists and
# fails if an entry here shadows a COPY there.

.git
.github
.venv
.resume
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.chroma
data/
.env
.env.railway
docs/
tests/
*.md

# S8.6 -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# scripts/ is dev + smoke tooling and does not belong in a runtime image. The
# one thing in there anyone might want in prod -- the retention sweep -- is not
# in there: it is `python -m app.retention.sweep`, inside the COPYed package,
# which is what lets the Railway cron call it (DEPLOY.md).
scripts/

# A 659KB paste screenshot from the 2026-08-03 UI session. Already gitignored,
# so it is local-only -- but the /ui mount serves whatever sits in frontend/,
# so without this line a developer's stray pastes are public on their machine.
#
# CORRECTED IN REVIEW: this comment used to claim the directory was fixture
# input for scripts/check_ui_screening_browser.py. It is not -- that script
# builds its fixtures in a scratch directory and never reads this one. The
# claim came from the S8.6 plan and was copied without checking.
frontend/uploads/
